{"id": "EUVD-2026-95427", "enisaUuid": "74c04fff-74bc-309d-97d7-366f56cf2e16", "description": "The HTTP/2 server can refund connection-level flow control twice for the same data: Once when a client resets a stream (refunding data for any sent-but-unread portion of the stream), and again when a request handler reads the buffered data. A malicious client can exploit this to bypass the configured connection-level flow control limit (MaxReceiveBufferPerConnection). Total buffered data is still limited by the concurrent stream limit and stream-level flow control.", "datePublished": "2026-10-08T22:53:59", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-09T16:42:50", "baseScore": 9.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://go.dev/cl/847187", "https://go.dev/cl/847310", "https://go.dev/issue/81743", "https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/U2fTuyDJznI", "https://groups.google.com/g/golang-announce/c/ZPwCyRUuGBs", "https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-6612"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-78663"], "assigner": "Go", "epss": 0.57, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "15f4c8dd-1450-3933-9bd4-8a63093e3fe5", "product": {"name": "net/http", "vendor": {"name": "Go standard library"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.26.9"}, {"id": "b52e953a-9db2-3506-b960-5ed3d235ce9e", "product": {"name": "golang.org/x/net/http2", "vendor": {"name": "golang.org/x/net"}}, "product_version": "0 <0.60.0"}, {"id": "f5d16562-45bf-349f-8f6b-7fbaf7305e1b", "product": {"name": "net/http/internal/http2", "vendor": {"name": "Go standard library"}}, "product_version": "1.27.0-0 <1.27.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1ac6991d-c763-3cf0-aebd-25a5b4d98736", "vendor": {"name": "Go standard library"}}, {"id": "a9227114-be1b-3e78-a07b-c338a4a3053f", "vendor": {"name": "golang.org/x/net"}}], "isExploited": false}